>> title: Lemon Curd
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: lemon, custard, spread, stovetop, make-ahead
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: lemon cheese, lemon spread
>> pairs-with: crepes
>> servings: 12
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: unforgiving — 170°F is the number and it is a narrow one: below it the curd never thickens, above it the eggs scramble and no straining hides the grain. It is stirred constantly because a curd left alone for ten seconds sets on the bottom of the pan first
>> step.2: whisk in the lemon
>> step.3: cook to 170°F (77°C), 8 min
>> step.4: beat in the butter

Whisk @egg yolks{6%large}(110 g), @eggs{2%large}(100 g), @granulated sugar{1%cup}(200 g), @table salt{1/4%tsp} in a #saucepan{} until pale.

Whisk @lemon juice{3/4%cup}(180 mL; 4 to 5 lemons), @lemon zest{2%tsp}(from 2 lemons) into @&(~1)eggs{}.

Cook @&(~1)mixture{} over medium-low, stirring constantly, until it thickens at 170°F (77°C), about ~{8%min}.

Beat @unsalted butter{6%Tbs}(85 g, cold and cubed) into @&(~1)hot curd{} a cube at a time.

Strain @&(~1)curd{} into a jar and chill for ~{3%hr}.
